1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,881
A mule pulls a cart up a hill road.

2
00:00:02,881 --> 00:00:05,140
It eats, breathes and gets tired.

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:08,744
A worker bee spends its whole
life working for the hive.

4
00:00:09,194 --> 00:00:11,763
Diya learnt something odd about both.

5
00:00:11,763 --> 00:00:13,590
A mule never has babies.

6
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:15,897
Most worker bees never lay eggs.

7
00:00:16,247 --> 00:00:18,160
Yet both are clearly alive.

8
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,069
So is making babies really a sign of life?

9
00:00:21,569 --> 00:00:26,164
Today we take four features of life,
one by one, and test each with its

10
00:00:26,164 --> 00:00:27,064
exceptions.

11
00:00:27,655 --> 00:00:30,469
Every feature faces
the same two questions.

12
00:00:30,819 --> 00:00:31,719
One.

13
00:00:31,304 --> 00:00:33,403
Does every living thing have it?

14
00:00:33,853 --> 00:00:34,753
Two.

15
00:00:34,381 --> 00:00:36,784
Does no non living thing have it?

16
00:00:36,784 --> 00:00:40,088
Only a feature that passes
both can define life.

17
00:00:40,738 --> 00:00:42,113
Feature one: growth.

18
00:00:42,463 --> 00:00:47,000
Growth means two things together:
more body mass, and more cells or more

19
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,900
individuals.

20
00:00:48,342 --> 00:00:51,064
A many celled body grows by cell division.

21
00:00:51,064 --> 00:00:53,632
One cell becomes two, two become four.

22
00:00:54,082 --> 00:00:56,831
Plants keep growing
this way all their life.

23
00:00:56,831 --> 00:00:59,299
Animals grow only up to a certain age.

24
00:00:59,749 --> 00:01:03,927
After that, cell division still
replaces worn out cells, like the skin

25
00:01:03,927 --> 00:01:04,827
you shed.

26
00:01:05,143 --> 00:01:09,740
But mountains, boulders and sand
mounds grow too, by piling material on

27
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:10,828
their surface.

28
00:01:11,278 --> 00:01:13,277
Living growth comes from inside.

29
00:01:13,277 --> 00:01:17,240
Still, since non living things
can grow, growth fails the test.

30
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:21,554
Feature two: reproduction, making
young ones like the parents.

31
00:01:21,904 --> 00:01:24,679
Many living things do
it without a partner.

32
00:01:24,679 --> 00:01:27,560
Yeast and hydra grow a
bud that breaks away.

33
00:01:28,010 --> 00:01:32,646
Cut a flatworm called Planaria into
pieces, and each piece grows into a

34
00:01:32,646 --> 00:01:33,867
whole new worm.

35
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:35,398
That is regeneration.

36
00:01:35,848 --> 00:01:40,315
Fungi, threadlike algae and the
protonema, the young thread stage of a

37
00:01:40,315 --> 00:01:43,752
moss, break into pieces,
and each piece lives on.

38
00:01:43,752 --> 00:01:45,281
That is fragmentation.

39
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:50,170
In one celled living things, like
bacteria, growing and reproducing are

40
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:53,086
the same event: one cell divides into two.

41
00:01:53,536 --> 00:01:58,394
But mules, worker bees and couples who
cannot have children never reproduce,

42
00:01:58,394 --> 00:01:59,861
and they are alive.

43
00:01:59,861 --> 00:02:01,419
So reproduction fails.

44
00:02:02,069 --> 00:02:04,037
Feature three: metabolism.

45
00:02:04,387 --> 00:02:08,416
Metabolism is the sum of all the
chemical reactions in a body.

46
00:02:08,416 --> 00:02:11,267
Food is broken down, new parts are built.

47
00:02:11,717 --> 00:02:16,470
Every living thing runs metabolism,
and no non living object does.

48
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:21,372
But scientists can run one of these
reactions in a test tube, with no cell

49
00:02:21,372 --> 00:02:22,272
at all.

50
00:02:22,047 --> 00:02:24,746
That tube is neither
living nor non living.

51
00:02:24,746 --> 00:02:26,386
It is a living reaction.

52
00:02:27,036 --> 00:02:31,689
So the real line is drawn by
feature four: cellular organisation.

53
00:02:31,689 --> 00:02:34,256
Life happens inside organised cells.

54
00:02:34,706 --> 00:02:36,896
And one more feature: response.

55
00:02:36,896 --> 00:02:40,310
Every living thing senses
its surroundings and reacts.

56
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,650
A shoot bends toward light.

57
00:02:42,650 --> 00:02:46,230
Day length tells many plants
and animals when to breed.

58
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:47,934
Humans go further.

59
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:49,679
We are aware of ourselves.

60
00:02:49,679 --> 00:02:51,414
That is self consciousness.

61
00:02:52,064 --> 00:02:53,865
Look at growth side by side.

62
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:58,553
A sand mound grows from outside,
as wind adds grains on top.

63
00:02:59,003 --> 00:03:03,057
A bean shoot grows from inside,
as its cells divide and swell.

64
00:03:03,657 --> 00:03:04,601
Your turn.

65
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,826
A worker bee cannot reproduce.

66
00:03:06,826 --> 00:03:08,280
Is it non living?

67
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,453
Yes, or no?

68
00:03:09,453 --> 00:03:10,842
Pause and decide.

69
00:03:14,042 --> 00:03:14,942
No!

70
00:03:14,519 --> 00:03:18,675
It is made of cells, its
metabolism runs, and it responds.

71
00:03:18,675 --> 00:03:23,504
Only reproduction is missing, and
reproduction is not a defining feature.

72
00:03:24,154 --> 00:03:25,284
Remember this.

73
00:03:25,284 --> 00:03:29,559
Every living thing has cells,
and runs metabolism inside them.

74
00:03:29,559 --> 00:03:30,636
No exception.

75
00:03:31,236 --> 00:03:32,963
Now, a worked example.

76
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,894
Four cases, four features.

77
00:03:35,244 --> 00:03:36,144
A mule.

78
00:03:36,066 --> 00:03:39,686
It grows, metabolises,
has cells and responds.

79
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:41,319
It cannot reproduce.

80
00:03:41,319 --> 00:03:42,483
Still living.

81
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:44,080
A sand mound.

82
00:03:44,080 --> 00:03:45,926
It grows, from outside.

83
00:03:45,926 --> 00:03:47,009
Nothing else.

84
00:03:47,009 --> 00:03:47,986
Non living.

85
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:50,329
A reaction in a test tube.

86
00:03:50,329 --> 00:03:52,153
Metabolism, but no cells.

87
00:03:52,153 --> 00:03:54,186
Neither living nor non living.

88
00:03:54,686 --> 00:03:56,246
A piece of Planaria.

89
00:03:56,246 --> 00:04:01,249
It has cells, metabolism and response,
and it regrows into a full worm.

90
00:04:01,249 --> 00:04:02,149
Living.

91
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:04,053
Now, the exam trap.

92
00:04:04,403 --> 00:04:08,566
Many students say: a metabolic
reaction in a test tube is living.

93
00:04:08,966 --> 00:04:10,417
But it has no cells.

94
00:04:10,417 --> 00:04:12,730
It is neither living nor non living.

95
00:04:12,730 --> 00:04:15,810
It is a living reaction,
outside a living thing.

96
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,878
Where is this asked?

97
00:04:17,878 --> 00:04:22,416
As match the column questions: each
way of reproduction with its organism.

98
00:04:23,016 --> 00:04:24,302
Exam level now.

99
00:04:24,302 --> 00:04:26,930
Match each method with its organism.

100
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,271
Pause and solve.

101
00:04:33,671 --> 00:04:35,046
The answer is B.

102
00:04:35,546 --> 00:04:37,008
Budding is yeast.

103
00:04:37,008 --> 00:04:38,926
Regeneration is Planaria.

104
00:04:39,426 --> 00:04:41,934
Fragmentation is the moss protonema.

105
00:04:41,934 --> 00:04:43,684
Spores belong to fungi.

106
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,740
Here is your recap.

107
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,237
Screenshot this card.

108
00:04:50,437 --> 00:04:53,274
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

109
00:04:53,674 --> 00:04:54,574
One.

110
00:04:54,164 --> 00:04:57,482
How is a sand mound's growth
different from a plant's?

111
00:04:58,382 --> 00:04:59,282
Two.

112
00:04:58,943 --> 00:05:02,954
Why can a mule not prove that
reproduction defines life?

113
00:05:03,854 --> 00:05:04,754
Three.

114
00:05:04,443 --> 00:05:07,343
Why is a reaction in
a test tube not alive?

115
00:05:08,443 --> 00:05:11,503
Next time: one walk
through the college garden.

116
00:05:11,503 --> 00:05:14,475
How many kinds of living
things can you count?

117
00:05:14,475 --> 00:05:18,179
We find out in biodiversity and
the need for classification.
